From 30fbea9463f71f3c4d1d26b98eda3d9f174820c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jcs130 <lzl1992@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:51:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tts): honor declared local stream completion across
 synthesis gaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

回归报告 / Regression Report

Natural VoxCPM2 playback still finished between sentences because the legacy
missing-audio_done fallback forced completion after only 700ms. Actual local
sentence synthesis gaps exceeded ten seconds, opening the proactive gate
before the original reply finished and causing more overlapping narration.

Declare the final audio_done contract in local-primary headers and forward
it to the frontend stream ledger. Only declared streams get a bounded 45s
missing-done grace, renewed by actual audio activity; their inter-sentence
gaps do not take the legacy 700ms or 30s sticky-speaking exit. Completion
still finalizes immediately and cancellation remains available. Unknown
providers retain the existing fallback. No model calls or text muting added.

The 700ms inter-sentence regression failed before the fix. Explicit missing
done recovery is also covered. Final related regression: 2130 passed, one
unchanged baseline logger-capture failure deselected. Ruff, Node syntax for
both playback and websocket modules, and diff checks pass. Natural playback
verification is separate and must reject early ends, not merely count final
acknowledgements. Both header producer and desktop consumer need this update.
